Verizon plans to charge customers &#36;10 per month for the iPhone Handoff feature <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/iphone-handoff-how-it-works-carrier-support-cost/">that Apple added in iOS 27</a>. iPhone Handoff allows one phone number to be shared across two separate iPhones.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062163" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-Handoff-Feature.jpeg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" /><br/>
Pricing was included in Verizon's <a href="https://www.verizon.com/about/news/iphone-duo-verizon-offers">iPhone Duo announcement today</a>, with the carrier confirming iPhone Handoff will work with the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> and the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> models.<br/>
<blockquote>Verizon will support iPhone Handoff, giving customers the flexibility to use a single Verizon phone number seamlessly across two compatible iPhone models. Whether using the pocketable iPhone Duo on the go or iPhone 18 Pro for work, customers can switch active status between devices at any time while keeping full access to Verizon's 5G network. iPhone Handoff will be available from Verizon for &#36;10/month on compatible iPhones models running iOS 27.</blockquote><br/>
With iPhone Handoff, users can switch between a main iPhone and a companion iPhone at will, though a phone number can only be active on one iPhone at a time. Verizon says support is "coming soon," and Apple previously said Verizon would adopt the feature before the end of the year.<br/>
<br/>
U.S. carrier T-Mobile already supports iPhone Handoff, but <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/10/ios-27-iphone-handoff-cost/">charges just &#36;5 per month</a> for the feature. AT&amp;T, the third major U.S. carrier, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/23/att-on-ios-27-iphone-handoff/">recently suggested</a> it has no imminent plans to support iPhone Handoff.<br/>
<br/>
U.K. carrier EE also said this week that it will <a href="https://newsroom.ee.co.uk/iphone-duo-with-iphone-handoff-only-on-ee/">soon support</a> iPhone Handoff. Customers who have EE's Full Works Plus plan will get iPhone Handoff free, while other EE users can get it for £5 per month.<br/>
<br/>
